  "term": "essential hypertension",
  "definition": "Essential hypertension is a common worldwide form of high blood pressure that is a major health problem. It is associated with a greater risk of coronary artery disease, cerebrovascular disease, and heart failure, and genetic variation in the vitamin D receptor has been linked to its development in some cases.",
